.TH EMERALD.REPO 5 "2026-09-07" "emerald" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
emerald.repo \- Emerald ports repository definitions
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/emerald.repo
lists local destinations and their Git remotes. Emerald and \fBportsync\fR use it to construct and synchronize the ports tree.
.SH FORMAT
Each non-empty, non-comment line contains up to three whitespace-separated fields:
.PP
.EX
REPOSITORY-DIRECTORY REMOTE-URL [BRANCH]
.EE
.PP
The branch defaults to \fBmain\fR when omitted. The destination may be absolute or use the configured ports directory.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
@PORTS_DIR@/core   https://gitlab.com/vylen/ports/core
@PORTS_DIR@/extra  https://gitlab.com/vylen/ports/extra dev
.EE
.PP
Lines beginning with \fB#\fR are disabled. The installed template may contain commented repositories for optional collections.
.SH MANAGEMENT
Run \fBportsync\fR to fetch and check out the configured repositories. Use its \fB--source\fR option to limit synchronization and \fB--reset\fR to recover a repository whose local state cannot be updated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR portsync (1),
.BR emerald (1)
